{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-95004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t+{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=3-t-3{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =2\\cdot (2t+{t}^{3})+2\\cdot (3-t-3{t}^{3}) \\\\  & =4t+2{t}^{3}+6-2t-6{t}^{3} \\\\  & =6+2t-4{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95004" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-95004" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.