(1+t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =-1-t-{t}^{2}+1+t-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106738" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-106738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2-2t"] ["math" "-2{t}^{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2+2t"] ["math" "{t}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106738" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2{t}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}+{t}^{3},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1+3{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =3\\cdot (2{t}^{2}+{t}^{3})+(-2)\\cdot (1+3{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}+3{t}^{3}-2-6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-2+3{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106734" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-106734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1+3{t}^{2}"] ["math" "-2+3{t}^{3}"] ["math" "-2-{t}^{3}"] ["math" "1+2{t}^{3}"] ["math" "1+7{t}^{2}+3{t}^{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106734" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2+3{t}^{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the polynomials ${p}_{1}(t)$ and ${p}_{2}(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $B$ are $[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any vector in  $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1},{p}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[p(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =1\\cdot (1-t+2{t}^{2})+3\\cdot (t-{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =1-t+2{t}^{2}+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =1+2t-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-95003" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95003" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "p(t)=1+2t-5{t}^{2}"] ["math" "p(t)=1+2t-6{t}^{2}"] ["math" "p(t)=1+2t-{t}^{2}"] ["math" "p(t)=1+4t-{t}^{2}"] ["math" "p(t)=1-3t-{t}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95003" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "p(t)=1+2t-{t}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106731" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{A}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{A}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices shown above. Find the matrix $C$ given that $B={{A}_{1},{A}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}},$ and the coordinates of the matrix $C$ relative to $B$ are $[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106731" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any vector in $\\text{Span}{{A}_{1},{A}_{2}}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{A}_{1}+{x}_{2}{A}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n[C]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =(-2)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106731" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-106731" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106731" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106731" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B={{B}_{1},{B}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} & -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{4}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{9}{2} & \\frac{9}{2} \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{5}{2} & -\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{9}{2}{x}_{2}=\\frac{9}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{2}{x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+6\\cdot 1 & =-2 \\\\ 4{x}_{1} & =-8 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-2+1=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-95016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$$\n{B}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{B}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nIf $B={{B}_{1},{B}_{2}}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{B}_{1},{B}_{2}},$ and $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} & -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 & -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ 9{x}_{2}=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+5\\cdot 1 & =4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}+1=\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-95019" 