quation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & -3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 9{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -6{x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{3} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy