te" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1} & 5{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{5}{4}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ From the first equation, we get ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-36587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderat