77208abd9"} {"question" "q-106754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{B}_{1}+{x}_{2}{B}_{2}=A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 & 2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} & -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 20 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=20 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 20 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{3}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 7{x}_{2}=14 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get ${x}_{2}=2.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 2 & =4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =8 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $[A]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+2=6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-106754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106754" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+{t}^{2},\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-t+2{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=6+2t.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(1-t+2{t}^{2}) & =6+2t \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})-{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =6+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{3}{2} & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=6 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$  Substituting this into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-2)=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+(-2)=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-106781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=-{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2{t}^{2}+4,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=3{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-3t+3,\\,\\,q(t)=-1.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{3}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(-{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+t)+{x}_{2}(2{t}^{2}+4)+{x}_{3}(3{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}-3t+3) & =-1 \\\\ (-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}){t}^{3}+({x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+({x}_{1}-3{x}_{3})t+(4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{4}+(-2){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}↔{R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -{x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}+2\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{3}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-95031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)={t}^{2}+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}-2t+4,\\,{p}_{3}(t)={t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-2,\\,\\,q(t)=2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}({t}^{2}+t)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}-2t+4)+{x}_{3}({t}^{3}-2{t}^{2}-2) & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3} \\\\ (4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3})+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})t+({x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+{x}_{3}{t}^{3} & =2+{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{3}{4}){R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 4{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n4{x}_{2}-2\\cdot 1=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2\\cdot 1=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{1}=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106835" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-106835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-106835" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2{t}^{2}+t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)={t}^{2}+3t-6,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2},\\,\\,q(t)=-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{2}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)+{x}_{3}{p}_{3}(t)=q(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2{t}^{2}+t-2)+{x}_{2}({t}^{2}+3t-6)+{x}_{3}(-2{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}{t}^{3}+(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}){t}^{2}+({x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})t+(-2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}) & =-2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+3t-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{2}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{3} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=1.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-5{x}_{2}+3\\cdot 1=-2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting the obtained values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+3\\cdot 1=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],$ and therefore ${x}_{2}=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95030" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-95030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95030" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2+t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=1-{t}^{2},\\,q(t)=2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nIf $B={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)}$ is a basis of $\\text{Span}{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)},$ and $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],$ then ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t)=q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(2+t)+{x}_{2}(1-{t}^{2}) & =2+3t+4{t}^{2} \\\\ (2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{1}t-{x}_{2}{t}^{2} & =2+3t+4{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{1}=3 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-4.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}+(-4)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[q(t)]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+(-4)=-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95023" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "26726781313c038b3332571ba963832974398ed5c9f14585bd40e94a76a1fe4a"} {"question" "q-95023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "q-95023" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd63bb404a88fb4be87a331845efedc2954b569b5c621d3d38605b677208abd9"} {"question" "e-8273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the polynomials $p_1(t)$ and $p_2(t),$ given by\n\n$$\np_1(t)=3+2t, \\qquad\n\tp_2(t)=-t+t^2.\n$$\n\nFind $p(t)$ given that $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\},$ and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/3274a690fa59f7d7368fcbe54004eab244c9845e20bf03ffce1e9fa25bbaf4bc.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/example-8273.json" "file_sha256" "e22a2d8c381a923c09a725ca3bf50957bc1156102e1b5bb1592de1f9a4fa11ab"} {"question" "e-8273" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{p}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}{p}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/170acd827e8b97471869159c5d9af88b0e4324b25ca1b42ec652011ece6a5174.png)\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(t) & =4\\cdot (3+2t)+(-3)\\cdot (-t+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =12+8t+3t-3{t}^{2} \\\\  & =12+11t-3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/example-8273.json" "file_sha256" "e22a2d8c381a923c09a725ca3bf50957bc1156102e1b5bb1592de1f9a4fa11ab"} {"question" "e-8274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following matrices:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/8a495251bb5d61eab1568624a6e1c213ccee49ec98fc8d5ff5c17fc841d027bf.png)\nIf $\\mathcal B = \\{B_1,B_2\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{ B_1, B_2 \\},$ calculate ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/342997674c65cf5c4d14f0b2a7df2649bf99a8b0c003be93efa983f317faa7a1.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/example-8274.json" "file_sha256" "c586999f4a455c0ae93c75dc657e29acc3623a3b6c791529ee889bdd88bdfb60"} {"question" "e-8274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 B_1 +x_2 B_2 = A.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & 0 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} & -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=-2 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/ebd814bcb627ef3b9208bc0960bdaf48b9448396ed7e95d18d8c4abbf1169244.png)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 18 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=18 \\\\ -{x}_{2}=-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get $x_2 =9.$ From the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-9 & =-5 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/dfc845ca1739c329e5636726466c76efee7eba19df4adc0909110506f894e72d.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/example-8274.json" "file_sha256" "c586999f4a455c0ae93c75dc657e29acc3623a3b6c791529ee889bdd88bdfb60"} {"question" "e-8275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$$\np_1(t)=5+t^2, \\quad\np_2(t)=3t-2t^2, \\quad\nq(t)=5-3t+3t^2.\n$$\n\nIf $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\},$ find $[q(t)]_{\\mathcal{B}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/example-8275.json" "file_sha256" "ea4599c3486521490d17ce34ab62679976b6a75d16d4194ab2b93987dcd31ed1"} {"question" "e-8275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\nx_1 p_1(t)+x_2 p_2(t) = q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(5+{t}^{2})+{x}_{2}(3t-2{t}^{2}) & =5-3t+3{t}^{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}t+({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}){t}^{2} & =5-3t+3{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/195a50f130cc40c4a725066035f2da3ef25b725df96601e53f70716bd82b4f4a.png)\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{5}){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}=5 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get $x_1=1$ and $x_2 =-1.$ Therefore, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/assets/9f23f71e833d7a7f81f511e1dfb72861ed753cb514de43d6cabfeb3c6b65fadb.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068026/example-8275.json" "file_sha256" "ea4599c3486521490d17ce34ab62679976b6a75d16d4194ab2b93987dcd31ed1"}] "usage" {"e-8273" [] "q-36587" [] "e-8275" [] "e-8274" []} "basis" 2495 "retractions" [[17592186167247 :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n\n$B_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, B_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, A = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nIf $B = {B_{1}, B_{2}}$ is a basis of $Span{B_{1}, B_{2}}$, and $[A]_{B} = \\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$, then $x_{1} + x_{2} =$"] [17592186166521 :question/problem "Consider the polynomials $p_1(t)$ and $p_2(t)$, given by\n$p_1(t)=3+2t, \\qquad p_2(t)=-t+t^2$.\nFind $p(t)$ given that $\\mathcal{B}=\\big\\{p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$, and the coordinates of $p(t)$ relative to $\\mathcal{B}$ are $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186166521 :question/worked-solution "Any vector in $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{p_1, p_2 \\big\\}$ can be written as\n\n$$\nx_{1}p_{1}(t) + x_{2}p_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\np(t) &= 4 \\cdot (3 + 2t) + (-3) \\cdot (-t + t^{2}) \\\\\n&= 12 + 8t + 3t - 3t^{2} \\\\\n&= 12 + 11t - 3t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186166522 :question/problem "Consider the following matrices:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\nIf $\\mathcal B = \\{B_1,B_2\\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\{B_1, B_2 \\}$, calculate $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186166522 :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that\n\n$$\nx_1 B_1 +x_2 B_2 = A\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -4\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}2x_{1} - x_{2} & 0 \\\\ 8x_{1} - 2x_{2} & -4x_{1} + x_{2}\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain\n\n$$\n{2x_{1} - x_{2} =-5; 8x_{1} - 2x_{2} =-2; - 4x_{1} + x_{2} = 1\n$$\n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nM = \\mid \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 8 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{2}:=R_{2} + (-4)R_{1} \\\\ R_{3}:=R_{3} + 2R_{1} \\\\ ∼\\end{vmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 18 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{2x_{1} - x_{2} =-5; 2x_{2} = 18; - x_{2} =-9\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we get $x_2 =9$. From the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x_{1} - 9 &= -5 \\\\\n2x_{1} &= 4 \\\\\nx_{1} &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186166523 :question/problem "Consider the following polynomials:\n\n$p_1(t)=5+t^2, \\quad p_2(t)=3t-2t^2, \\quad q(t)=5-3t+3t^2$.\n\nIf $\\mathcal{B}=\\{p_1(t), p_2(t) \\}$ is a basis of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{p_1(t), p_2(t) \\big\\}$, find $[q(t)]_{\\mathcal{B}}$."] [17592186166523 :question/worked-solution "We need to find $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that\n\n$$\nx_1 p_1(t)+x_2 p_2(t) = q(t)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given information into the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}(5 + t^{2}) + x_{2}(3t - 2t^{2}) &= 5 - 3t + 3t^{2} \\\\\n5x_{1} + 3x_{2}t + (x_{1} - 2x_{2})t^{2} &= 5 - 3t + 3t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $t$, we obtain\n\n$$\n{5x_{1} = 5; 3x_{2} =-3; x_{1} - 2x_{2} = 3\n$$\n\nThe equations above give a linear system with the augmented matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the matrix using Gaussian elimination, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nM =\\begin{vmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3} &:=R_{3} + (-\\frac{1}{5})R_{1} \\\\ ∼ & \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + \\frac{2}{3}R_{2}; ∼ \\mid \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{5x_{1} = 5; 3x_{2} =-3\n$$\n\nFrom the first and second equations, we get $x_1=1$ and $x_2 =-1$. Therefore, $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186165032 17592186165033 17592186165034 17592186165035 17592186165036] "immutable_fields" [[17592186165031 :answer-field/correct] [17592186165031 :answer-field/id] [17592186165031 :answer-field/key] [17592186165031 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
